---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Autoflowering"
letter: "A"
anchor: "autoflowering"
category: "growing"
---

A cannabis plant that flowers based on age rather than changes in light cycle. Standard (photoperiod) cannabis plants flower when they receive 12 hours of darkness per day — autoflowering plants flower automatically after a set number of weeks regardless of light schedule. Autoflowering strains contain *Cannabis ruderalis* genetics and are generally faster, smaller, and more forgiving for beginner growers. The tradeoff is typically lower yield and less potency than equivalent photoperiod strains.
